   "source": [
    "<div style=\"border-top:4px solid #0f766e;padding:16px\">DATA WAREHOUSING WITH APACHE DORIS · OPTIONAL LAB</div>\n",
    "\n",
    "# Optional Lab 5A: Kafka → Routine Load → Doris\n",
    "\n",
    "Consume order JSON continuously, inspect progress, pause consumption to build a backlog, then resume and verify the results.\n",
    "Allow 25–40 minutes. This lab is not required to complete Level 1.\n",
    "\n",
    "Read the [environment guide](../../environments/streaming/README.md) first. You need Docker Compose, download access, and the course Python environment. This is a local test environment only.\n",
    "The first cell checks Docker capacity and applies the streaming resource overlay (12 GiB Doris memory cap). Applying the overlay to an existing sandbox may recreate its container while preserving its named volumes: finish other course work first.\n",
    "The lab starts Doris and Kafka and rebuilds only `dw_course_l1_streaming.ext_kafka_orders`.\n",
    "It leaves the main course order tables unchanged. Each run uses a new topic and job; run only one instance of this lab per sandbox.\n",
    "\n",
    "The input contains simulated business orders, not MySQL Binlog events. Events are sent in order to a single partition; cross-partition reordering is not tested."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "d72511e1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import os, sys\n",
    "from uuid import uuid4\n",
    "course = next(p for p in [Path.cwd(), *Path.cwd().parents] if (p / \"dw_course\").is_dir())\n",
    "sys.path.insert(0, str(course))\n",
    "from dw_course.docker_runtime import prepare_environment, connect_sandbox\n",
    "from dw_course.runtime import expect\n",
    "from dw_course.streaming import (\n",
    "    prepare_streaming, kafka, produce, mysql, flink_api, submit_sql,\n",
    "    wait_checkpoint, stop_with_savepoint, wait_rows, check_flink_job, check_routine_load,\n",
    "    cleanup_kafka_routine_load,\n",
    ")\n",
    "prepare_environment(start=True, streaming=True, streaming_profile="kafka")\n",
    "os.environ[\"DW_DATABASE\"] = \"dw_course_l1_streaming\"\n",
    "lab = connect_sandbox()\n",
    "print(\"Isolated lab database:\", lab.database)\n",
    "\n",
    "prepare_streaming(\"kafka\", start=True)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f24cd777",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Create the target table, topic, and continuous load job\n",
    "\n",
    "The setup cell automatically stops stale jobs created by this lab after checking their name and target table. It refuses to touch any unrelated Routine Load job. Never rebuild a table while an unrecognized job is consuming data.\n",
    "Doris manages Routine Load progress; it is not a regular Kafka consumer group's committed offset."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "40048154",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "cleanup_kafka_routine_load(lab)\n",
    "expect(lab.query(\"SHOW ROUTINE LOAD\"), [])\n",
    "lab.execute(\"DROP TABLE IF EXISTS ext_kafka_orders\")\n",
    "lab.execute(\"\"\"CREATE TABLE ext_kafka_orders (\n",
    "    order_id BIGINT NOT NULL, customer_id BIGINT NOT NULL,\n",
    "    order_status VARCHAR(32) NOT NULL, order_amount DECIMAL(18,2) NOT NULL\n",
    ") UNIQUE KEY(order_id) DISTRIBUTED BY HASH(order_id) BUCKETS 1\n",
    "PROPERTIES(\"replication_num\"=\"1\", \"enable_unique_key_merge_on_write\"=\"true\")\"\"\")\n",
    "run_id = uuid4().hex[:12]\n",
    "topic = \"course_orders_\" + run_id\n",
    "job_name = \"course_orders_\" + run_id\n",
    "print(kafka(\"kafka-topics.sh\", \"--create\", \"--topic\", topic, \"--partitions\", \"1\", \"--replication-factor\", \"1\"))\n",
    "load_sql = f'''CREATE ROUTINE LOAD {job_name} ON ext_kafka_orders\n",
    "COLUMNS(order_id, customer_id, order_status, order_amount)\n",
    "PROPERTIES(\"format\"=\"json\", \"desired_concurrent_number\"=\"1\",\n",
    "           \"max_batch_interval\"=\"5\", \"max_error_number\"=\"0\", \"strict_mode\"=\"true\")\n",
    "FROM KAFKA(\"kafka_broker_list\"=\"course-stream-kafka:9092\", \"kafka_topic\"=\"{topic}\",\n",
    "           \"property.kafka_default_offsets\"=\"OFFSET_BEGINNING\")'''\n",
    "print(load_sql)\n",
    "lab.execute(load_sql)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "8a407a74",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Send two orders and wait for query visibility\n",
    "\n",
    "Successful publication does not mean the rows are already visible in Doris. Polling has a timeout and checks the load job on every attempt. An unexpected pause or terminal state reports the job name, reason, and error URLs. Do not skip result validation."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "6527caab",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "rows = [dict(order_id=910001, customer_id=1, order_status=\"CREATED\", order_amount=\"100.00\"),\n",
    "        dict(order_id=910002, customer_id=2, order_status=\"CREATED\", order_amount=\"200.00\")]\n",
    "produce(topic, rows)\n",
    "baseline = [[910001,1,\"CREATED\",\"100.00\"],[910002,2,\"CREATED\",\"200.00\"]]\n",
    "expect(wait_rows(lab,\"ext_kafka_orders\",baseline, check_health=lambda: check_routine_load(lab, job_name), description=\"initial Kafka rows\"), baseline)\n",
    "lab.sql(f\"SHOW ROUTINE LOAD FOR {job_name}\", title=\"Consumption state and progress\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "af8c877b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Pause consumption and build a backlog\n",
    "\n",
    "Pause the job and record committed progress before sending the third order. After two batch intervals, the table should be unchanged.\n",
    "Pausing does not undo committed data. Verify the baseline first so earlier in-flight data is not mistaken for a new arrival."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "995bba8d",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import time\n",
    "lab.execute(f\"PAUSE ROUTINE LOAD FOR {job_name}\")\n",
    "paused = lab.sql(f\"SHOW ROUTINE LOAD FOR {job_name}\")\n",
    "expect(paused.iloc[0][\"State\"], \"PAUSED\")\n",
    "produce(topic,[dict(order_id=910003,customer_id=3,order_status=\"CREATED\",order_amount=\"50.00\")])\n",
    "time.sleep(12)\n",
    "expect(lab.query(\"SELECT * FROM ext_kafka_orders ORDER BY order_id\"), baseline)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "22f4eef8",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Resume consumption, then send a duplicate and an update\n",
    "\n",
    "Unique Key keeps the current state of each order, not its full business history. Repeated orders do not increase the logical row count.\n",
    "This does not establish end-to-end exactly-once behavior under arbitrary failures. See Module 7 for out-of-order version arbitration."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "2264e1db",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "lab.execute(f\"RESUME ROUTINE LOAD FOR {job_name}\")\n",
    "expected = baseline + [[910003,3,\"CREATED\",\"50.00\"]]\n",
    "expect(wait_rows(lab,\"ext_kafka_orders\",expected, check_health=lambda: check_routine_load(lab, job_name), description=\"new row after resume\"),expected)\n",
    "produce(topic,[rows[0],dict(order_id=910001,customer_id=1,order_status=\"PAID\",order_amount=\"100.00\")])\n",
    "expected[0][2] = \"PAID\"\n",
    "expect(wait_rows(lab,\"ext_kafka_orders\",expected, check_health=lambda: check_routine_load(lab, job_name), description=\"updated order after resume\"),expected)\n",
    "lab.sql(f\"SHOW ROUTINE LOAD FOR {job_name}\", title=\"Progress after resuming\")\n",
    "expect(lab.query(\"SELECT COUNT(*),SUM(order_amount) FROM ext_kafka_orders\"), [[3,\"350.00\"]])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "3312b4f7",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Stop the job and retain the results\n",
    "\n",
    "Acceptance: two rows during the pause; three rows totaling 350.00 after resuming; order 910001 is PAID. Submit screenshots of progress before and after the pause.\n",
    "STOP is terminal, unlike a resumable PAUSE. Delete only this run's dedicated topic; retain the Doris results.\n",
    "\n",
    "Independent exercise: create a separate topic and target table, combine `max_error_number=0` with an invalid amount, and inspect the job state and error reason. Do not introduce bad data into the current baseline."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "c4c9b1ab",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "lab.execute(f\"STOP ROUTINE LOAD FOR {job_name}\")\n",
    "print(kafka(\"kafka-topics.sh\", \"--delete\", \"--topic\", topic))\n",
    "lab.close()"
   ]
  }
 ],
